	'messages:apihelp-undelete-summary' => 'en:Undelete revisions of a deleted page.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-extended-description' => 'en:A list of deleted revisions (including timestamps) can be retrieved through [[Special:ApiHelp/query+deletedrevisions|prop=deletedrevisions]], and a list of deleted file IDs can be retrieved through [[Special:ApiHelp/query+filearchive|list=filearchive]].',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-title' => 'en:Title of the page to undelete.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-reason' => 'en:Reason for restoring.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-tags' => 'en:Change tags to apply to the entry in the deletion log.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-timestamps' => 'en:Timestamps of the revisions to undelete. If both <var>$1timestamps</var> and <var>$1fileids</var> are empty, all will be undeleted.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-fileids' => 'en:IDs of the file revisions to restore. If both <var>$1timestamps</var> and <var>$1fileids</var> are empty, all will be restored.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-watchlist' => 'en:Unconditionally add or remove the page from the current user\'s watchlist, use preferences (ignored for bot users) or do not change watch.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-watchlistexpiry' => 'en:Watchlist expiry timestamp. Omit this parameter entirely to leave the current expiry unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-param-undeletetalk' => 'en:Undelete all revisions of the associated talk page, if any.',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-example-page' => 'en:Undelete page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]].',
	'messages:apihelp-undelete-example-revisions' => 'en:Undelete two revisions of page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]].',
	'messages:apihelp-unlinkaccount-summary' => 'en:Remove a linked third-party account from the current user.',
	'messages:apihelp-unlinkaccount-example-simple' => 'en:Attempt to remove the current user\'s link for the provider associated with <kbd>FooAuthenticationRequest</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-summary' => 'en:Upload a file, or get the status of pending uploads.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-extended-description' => 'en:Several methods are available:
* Upload file contents directly, using the <var>$1file</var> parameter.
* Upload the file in pieces, using the <var>$1filesize</var>, <var>$1chunk</var>, and <var>$1offset</var> parameters.
* Have the MediaWiki server fetch a file from a URL, using the <var>$1url</var> parameter.
* Complete an earlier upload that failed due to warnings, using the <var>$1filekey</var> parameter.
Note that the HTTP POST must be done as a file upload (i.e. using <code>multipart/form-data</code>) when sending the <var>$1file</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-filename' => 'en:Target filename.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-comment' => 'en:Upload comment. Also used as the initial page text for new files if <var>$1text</var> is not specified.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-tags' => 'en:Change tags to apply to the upload log entry and file page revision.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-text' => 'en:Initial page text for new files.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-watch' => 'en:Watch the page.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-watchlist' => 'en:Unconditionally add or remove the page from the current user\'s watchlist, use preferences (ignored for bot users) or do not change watch.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-watchlistexpiry' => 'en:Watchlist expiry timestamp. Omit this parameter entirely to leave the current expiry unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-ignorewarnings' => 'en:Ignore any warnings.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-file' => 'en:File contents.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-url' => 'en:URL to fetch the file from.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-filekey' => 'en:Key that identifies a previous upload that was stashed temporarily.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-sessionkey' => 'en:Same as $1filekey, maintained for backward compatibility.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-stash' => 'en:If set, the server will stash the file temporarily instead of adding it to the repository.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-filesize' => 'en:Filesize of entire upload.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-offset' => 'en:Offset of chunk in bytes.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-chunk' => 'en:Chunk contents.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-async' => 'en:Make potentially large file operations asynchronous when possible.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-param-checkstatus' => 'en:Only fetch the upload status for the given file key.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-example-url' => 'en:Upload from a URL.',
	'messages:apihelp-upload-example-filekey' => 'en:Complete an upload that failed due to warnings.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-summary' => 'en:Change a user\'s group membership.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-user' => 'en:User.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-add' => 'en:Add the user to these groups, or if they are already a member, update the expiry of their membership in that group.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-expiry' => 'en:Expiry timestamps. May be relative (e.g. <kbd>5 months</kbd> or <kbd>2 weeks</kbd>) or absolute (e.g. <kbd>2014-09-18T12:34:56Z</kbd>). If only one timestamp is set, it will be used for all groups passed to the <var>$1add</var> parameter. Use <kbd>infinite</kbd>, <kbd>indefinite</kbd>, <kbd>infinity</kbd>, or <kbd>never</kbd> for a never-expiring user group.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-remove' => 'en:Remove the user from these groups.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-reason' => 'en:Reason for the change.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-tags' => 'en:Change tags to apply to the entry in the user rights log.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-watchuser' => 'en:Watch the user\'s user and talk pages.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-param-watchlistexpiry' => 'en:Watchlist expiry timestamp. Omit this parameter entirely to leave the current expiry unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-example-user' => 'en:Add user <kbd>FooBot</kbd> to group <kbd>bot</kbd>, and remove from groups <kbd>sysop</kbd> and <kbd>bureaucrat</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-example-userid' => 'en:Add the user with ID <kbd>123</kbd> to group <kbd>bot</kbd>, and remove from groups <kbd>sysop</kbd> and <kbd>bureaucrat</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-userrights-example-expiry' => 'en:Add user <kbd>SometimeSysop</kbd> to group <kbd>sysop</kbd> for 1 month.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-summary' => 'en:Validate a password against the wiki\'s password policies.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-extended-description' => 'en:Validity is reported as <samp>Good</samp> if the password is acceptable, <samp>Change</samp> if the password may be used for login but must be changed, or <samp>Invalid</samp> if the password is not usable.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-param-password' => 'en:Password to validate.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-param-user' => 'en:Username, for use when testing account creation. The named user must not exist.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-param-email' => 'en:Email address, for use when testing account creation.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-param-realname' => 'en:Real name, for use when testing account creation.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-example-1' => 'en:Validate the password <kbd>foobar</kbd> for the current user.',
	'messages:apihelp-validatepassword-example-2' => 'en:Validate the password <kbd>qwerty</kbd> for creating user <kbd>Example</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-summary' => 'en:Add or remove pages from the current user\'s watchlist.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-param-title' => 'en:The page to (un)watch. Use <var>$1titles</var> instead.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-param-expiry' => 'en:Expiry timestamp to be applied to all given pages. Omit this parameter entirely to leave any current expiries unchanged.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-param-unwatch' => 'en:If set the page will be unwatched rather than watched.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-example-watch' => 'en:Watch the page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]].',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-example-watch-expiry' => 'en:Watch the pages [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]], <kbd>Foo</kbd>, and <kbd>Bar</kbd> for one month.',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-example-unwatch' => 'en:Unwatch the page [[{{MediaWiki:Mainpage}}]].',
	'messages:apihelp-watch-example-generator' => 'en:Watch the first few pages in the main namespace.',
	'messages:apihelp-format-example-generic' => 'en:Return the query result in the $1 format.',
	'messages:apihelp-format-param-wrappedhtml' => 'en:Return the pretty-printed HTML and associated ResourceLoader modules as a JSON object.',
	'messages:apihelp-json-param-callback' => 'en:If specified, wraps the output into a given function call. For safety, all user-specific data will be restricted.',
	'messages:apihelp-json-param-ascii' => 'en:If specified, encodes all non-ASCII using hexadecimal escape sequences. Default when <var>formatversion</var> is <kbd>1</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-json-param-formatversion' => 'en:Output formatting',
	'messages:apihelp-json-paramvalue-formatversion-1' => 'en:Backwards-compatible format (XML-style booleans, <samp>*</samp> keys for content nodes, etc.).',
	'messages:apihelp-json-paramvalue-formatversion-2' => 'en:Modern format.',
	'messages:apihelp-json-paramvalue-formatversion-latest' => 'en:Use the latest format (currently <kbd>2</kbd>), may change without warning.',
	'messages:apihelp-none-summary' => 'en:Output nothing.',
	'messages:apihelp-php-param-formatversion' => 'en:Output formatting',
	'messages:apihelp-php-paramvalue-formatversion-1' => 'en:Backwards-compatible format (XML-style booleans, <samp>*</samp> keys for content nodes, etc.).',
	'messages:apihelp-php-paramvalue-formatversion-2' => 'en:Modern format.',
	'messages:apihelp-php-paramvalue-formatversion-latest' => 'en:Use the latest format (currently <kbd>2</kbd>), may change without warning.',
	'messages:apihelp-phpfm-summary' => 'en:Output data in serialized PHP format (pretty-print in HTML).',
	'messages:apihelp-rawfm-summary' => 'en:Output data, including debugging elements, in JSON format (pretty-print in HTML).',
	'messages:apihelp-xml-param-xslt' => 'en:If specified, adds the named page as an XSL stylesheet. The value must be a title in the {{ns:MediaWiki}} namespace ending in <code>.xsl</code>.',
	'messages:apihelp-xml-param-includexmlnamespace' => 'en:If specified, adds an XML namespace.',
	'messages:api-format-prettyprint-header-only-html' => 'en:This is an HTML representation intended for debugging, and is unsuitable for application use.

See the [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/API|complete documentation]], or the [[Special:ApiHelp/main|API help]] for more information.',
	'messages:api-format-prettyprint-header-hyperlinked' => 'en:This is the HTML representation of the $1 format. HTML is good for debugging, but is unsuitable for application use.

Specify the <var>format</var> parameter to change the output format. To see the non-HTML representation of the $1 format, set [$3 <kbd>format=$2</kbd>].

See the [[mw:API|complete documentation]], or the [[Special:ApiHelp/main|API help]] for more information.',
	'messages:api-format-prettyprint-status' => 'en:This response would be returned with HTTP status $1 $2.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-aborted' => 'en:Authentication requires user interaction, which is not supported by <kbd>action=login</kbd>. To be able to login with <kbd>action=login</kbd>, see [[Special:BotPasswords]]. To continue using main-account login, see <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/clientlogin|action=clientlogin]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-aborted-nobotpw' => 'en:Authentication requires user interaction, which is not supported by <kbd>action=login</kbd>. To log in, see <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/clientlogin|action=clientlogin]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-badsessionprovider' => 'en:Cannot log in when using $1.',
	'messages:api-login-fail-sameorigin' => 'en:Cannot log in when the same-origin policy is not applied.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-titles' => 'en:A list of titles to work on.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-pageids' => 'en:A list of page IDs to work on.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-revids' => 'en:A list of revision IDs to work on. Note that almost all query modules will convert revision IDs to the corresponding page ID and work on the latest revision instead. Only <kbd>prop=revisions</kbd> uses exact revisions for its response.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-generator' => 'en:Get the list of pages to work on by executing the specified query module.

<strong>Note:</strong> Generator parameter names must be prefixed with a "g", see examples.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-redirects-generator' => 'en:Automatically resolve redirects in <var>$1titles</var>, <var>$1pageids</var>, and <var>$1revids</var>, and in pages returned by <var>$1generator</var>.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-redirects-nogenerator' => 'en:Automatically resolve redirects in <var>$1titles</var>, <var>$1pageids</var>, and <var>$1revids</var>.',
	'messages:api-pageset-param-converttitles' => 'en:Convert titles to other variants if necessary. Only works if the wiki\'s content language supports variant conversion. Languages that support variant conversion include $1.',
	'messages:api-help-undocumented-module' => 'en:No documentation for module $1.',
	'messages:api-help-flags' => 'en:',
	'messages:api-help-source' => 'en:Source: $1',
	'messages:api-help-source-unknown' => 'en:Source: <span class="apihelp-unknown">unknown</span>',
	'messages:api-help-license' => 'en:License: [[$1|$2]]',
	'messages:api-help-license-noname' => 'en:License: [[$1|See link]]',
	'messages:api-help-license-unknown' => 'en:License: <span class="apihelp-unknown">unknown</span>',
	'messages:api-help-help-urls' => 'en:',
	'messages:api-help-parameters-note' => 'en:Other general parameters are available.',
	'messages:api-help-param-deprecated-label' => 'en:deprecated',
	'messages:api-help-param-internal' => 'en:Internal.',
	'messages:api-help-param-internal-label' => 'en:internal',
	'messages:api-help-param-templated' => 'en:This is a [[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/templatedparams|templated parameter]]. When making the request, $2.',
	'messages:api-help-param-templated-var-first' => 'en:<var>&#x7B;$1&#x7D;</var> in the parameter\'s name should be replaced with values of <var>$2</var>',
	'messages:api-help-param-templated-var' => 'en:<var>&#x7B;$1&#x7D;</var> with values of <var>$2</var>',
	'messages:api-help-datatypes-header' => 'en:Data types',
	'messages:api-help-datatypes-top' => 'en:Input to MediaWiki should be NFC-normalized UTF-8. MediaWiki may attempt to convert other input, but this may cause some operations (such as [[Special:ApiHelp/edit|edits]] with MD5 checks) to fail.

Parameters that take multiple values are normally submitted with the values separated using the pipe character, e.g. <kbd>param=value1|value2</kbd> or <kbd>param=value1%7Cvalue2</kbd>. If a value must contain the pipe character, use U+001F (Unit Separator) as the separator \'\'and\'\' prefix the value with U+001F, e.g. <kbd>param=%1Fvalue1%1Fvalue2</kbd>.

Some parameter types in API requests need further explanation:',
	'messages:api-help-datatype-boolean' => 'en:Boolean parameters work like HTML checkboxes: if the parameter is specified, regardless of value, it is considered true. For a false value, omit the parameter entirely.',
	'messages:api-help-datatype-expiry' => 'en:Expiry values may be relative (e.g. <kbd>5 months</kbd> or <kbd>2 weeks</kbd>) or absolute (e.g. <kbd>2014-09-18T12:34:56Z</kbd>). For no expiry, use <kbd>infinite</kbd>, <kbd>indefinite</kbd>, <kbd>infinity</kbd> or <kbd>never</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-help-datatype-timestamp' => 'en:Timestamps may be specified in several formats, see [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Timestamp|the Timestamp library input formats documented on mediawiki.org]] for details. ISO 8601 date and time is recommended: <kbd><var>2001</var>-<var>01</var>-<var>15</var>T<var>14</var>:<var>56</var>:<var>00</var>Z</kbd>. Additionally, the string <kbd>now</kbd> may be used to specify the current timestamp.',
	'messages:api-help-templatedparams-header' => 'en:Templated parameters',
	'messages:api-help-templatedparams' => 'en:Templated parameters support cases where an API module needs a value for each value of some other parameter. For example, if there were an API module to request fruit, it might have a parameter <var>fruits</var> to specify which fruits are being requested and a templated parameter <var>{fruit}-quantity</var> to specify how many of each fruit to request. An API client that wants 1 apple, 5 bananas, and 20 strawberries could then make a request like <kbd>fruits=apples|bananas|strawberries&apples-quantity=1&bananas-quantity=5&strawberries-quantity=20</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-help-param-type-expiry' => 'en:Type: {{PLURAL:$1|1=expiry|2=list of expiries}} ([[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/datatype/expiry|details]])',
	'messages:api-help-param-type-limit' => 'en:Type: integer or <kbd>max</kbd>',
	'messages:api-help-param-type-presenceboolean' => 'en:Type: boolean ([[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/datatype/boolean|details]])',
	'messages:api-help-param-type-timestamp' => 'en:Type: {{PLURAL:$1|1=timestamp|2=list of timestamps}} ([[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/datatype/timestamp|allowed formats]])',
	'messages:api-help-param-type-enum' => 'en:{{PLURAL:$1|1=One of the following values|2=Values (separate with <kbd>{{!}}</kbd> or [[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/datatypes|alternative]])}}: $2',
	'messages:api-help-param-multi-all' => 'en:To specify all values, use <kbd>$1</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-help-param-token' => 'en:A "$1" token retrieved from [[Special:ApiHelp/query+tokens|action=query&meta=tokens]]',
	'messages:api-help-param-token-webui' => 'en:For compatibility, the token used in the web UI is also accepted.',
	'messages:api-help-param-disabled-in-miser-mode' => 'en:Disabled due to [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgMiserMode|miser mode]].',
	'messages:api-help-param-limited-in-miser-mode' => 'en:<strong>Note:</strong> Due to [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:$wgMiserMode|miser mode]], using this may result in fewer than <var>$1limit</var> results returned before continuing; in extreme cases, zero results may be returned.',
	'messages:api-help-param-direction' => 'en:In which direction to enumerate:',
	'messages:api-help-paramvalue-direction-newer' => 'en:List oldest first. Note: $1start has to be before $1end.',
	'messages:api-help-paramvalue-direction-older' => 'en:List newest first (default). Note: $1start has to be later than $1end.',
	'messages:api-help-param-continue' => 'en:When more results are available, use this to continue. More detailed information on how to continue queries [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/API:Continue|can be found on mediawiki.org]].',
	'messages:api-help-right-apihighlimits' => 'en:Use higher limits in API queries (slow queries: $1; fast queries: $2). The limits for slow queries also apply to multivalue parameters.',
	'messages:api-help-open-in-apisandbox' => 'en:<small>[open in sandbox]</small>',
	'messages:api-help-no-extended-description' => 'en:',
	'messages:api-help-authmanager-general-usage' => 'en:The general procedure to use this module is:
# Fetch the fields available from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$4</kbd>, and a <kbd>$5</kbd> token from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+tokens|action=query&meta=tokens]]</kbd>.
# Present the fields to the user, and obtain their submission.
# Post to this module, supplying <var>$1returnurl</var> and any relevant fields.
# Check the <samp>status</samp> in the response.
#* If you received <samp>PASS</samp> or <samp>FAIL</samp>, you\'re done. The operation either succeeded or it didn\'t.
#* If you received <samp>UI</samp>, present the new fields to the user and obtain their submission. Then post to this module with <var>$1continue</var> and the relevant fields set, and repeat step 4.
#* If you received <samp>REDIRECT</samp>, direct the user to the <samp>redirecttarget</samp> and wait for the return to <var>$1returnurl</var>. Then post to this module with <var>$1continue</var> and any fields passed to the return URL, and repeat step 4.
#* If you received <samp>RESTART</samp>, that means the authentication worked but we don\'t have a linked user account. You might treat this as <samp>UI</samp> or as <samp>FAIL</samp>.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-requests' => 'en:Only use these authentication requests, by the <samp>id</samp> returned from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$1</kbd> or from a previous response from this module.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-request' => 'en:Use this authentication request, by the <samp>id</samp> returned from <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$1</kbd>.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-messageformat' => 'en:Format to use for returning messages.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-mergerequestfields' => 'en:Merge field information for all authentication requests into one array.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-preservestate' => 'en:Preserve state from a previous failed login attempt, if possible.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-returnurl' => 'en:Return URL for third-party authentication flows, must be absolute. Either this or <var>$1continue</var> is required.

Upon receiving a <samp>REDIRECT</samp> response, you will typically open a browser or web view to the specified <samp>redirecttarget</samp> URL for a third-party authentication flow. When that completes, the third party will send the browser or web view to this URL. You should extract any query or POST parameters from the URL and pass them as a <var>$1continue</var> request to this API module.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-continue' => 'en:This request is a continuation after an earlier <samp>UI</samp> or <samp>REDIRECT</samp> response. Either this or <var>$1returnurl</var> is required.',
	'messages:api-help-authmanagerhelper-additional-params' => 'en:This module accepts additional parameters depending on the available authentication requests. Use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> with <kbd>amirequestsfor=$1</kbd> (or a previous response from this module, if applicable) to determine the requests available and the fields that they use.',
